cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the paper for the formal result and the evidence archive when referring to the recorded mainnet execution."
title: "Aspis: End-to-End Formal Verification of a Transparent Private Spend on Solana"
type: software
version: "5"
date-released: 2026-08-24
authors:
  - family-names: "Barker"
    given-names: "Dominic"
    website: "https://github.com/DJBarker87"
abstract: >-
  Aspis provides an end-to-end Lean proof for every successful execution of a
  transparent private-spend verifier on Solana. Starting from the translated
  deployed Rust path, the proof derives the parse, Fiat-Shamir transcript, six
  work checks, 18 distinct queries, five authenticated opening sections, four
  low-degree folds, final polynomial, complete algebraic claim data, and both
  final accumulators from the same call. The 331-module replay is paired with
  pinned translation inputs, a byte-reproducible 1,258,496-byte Solana
  program, and a finalized mainnet transaction that verified a 75,358-byte
  proof in 1,334,452 compute units. The paper proves a conditional
  work-normalized security bound and reports raw post-grind accounting
  separately. Published decoding and Fiat-Shamir results, concrete primitive
  security, toolchain correctness, and Solana runtime behavior are explicit
  assumptions.
keywords:
  - "zero knowledge"
  - "transparent arguments"
  - "Solana"
  - "STARK"
  - "WHIR"
  - "M31"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "Aeneas"
  - "formal verification"
  - "reproducible builds"
